! CODE V TRA: transmission analysis -- per field and wavelength, the mean
! over the rays reaching the image of the surface losses (coating, else
! bare Fresnel), the bulk absorption (glass catalog IT data) and both.
RES osdtriplet
! one ray (the axial chief ray), checked by hand: the six bare surfaces
! give 0.707496 (normal-incidence Fresnel at n 1.62041 and 1.62005); the
! bulk, 7 mm of N-SK16 and 1.5 mm of N-F2 from Schott's IT data
TRA
NRD 1
GO
! the default grid (20 across); fields after the first give the weighted
! line only, unless FUL Y
TRA
GO
TRA
FUL Y
NRD 10
GO
! options that are refused
TRA
PLI Y
NRD 0
CAN
! a mirror is lossless; a SPECIAL material without IT data has no bulk loss
LEN NEW
EPD  20
TIT 'OSDmirror'
RDY S1 -100
PIM
RMD S1 REFL
TRA
NRD 4
GO
CV2PRG LithoKotaro.seq
TRA
NRD 4
GO
! SET ABS Y: the same bulk absorption in the ray energy of the other
! analyses (spot % transmission = TRA's weighted bulk figure, 0.996361),
! saved with the lens and cleared by a new lens; the engine and the legacy
! tracer agree
RES osdtriplet
SPD
SET ABS
SET ABS Y
SPD
SAV absrt
RES absrt
SET ABS
RAYENGINE CHECK
CAPFN 32
RAYENGINE OFF
SPD
RAYENGINE ON
LEN NEW
SET ABS
SET ABS MAYBE
